---
// The qualities that don't film — they're about what DOESN'T happen (no
// spinner, no reload, no cloud round-trip) — stated plainly as a quiet
// strip instead of pretending to be scenes. Every claim here is literal app
// behavior: cache-first paint with 60s/focus refresh, session resume,
// review-request toasts, and a token that never leaves the Rust backend.
---

<section class="wide locals" aria-label="Local-first qualities">
  <h2 class="locals__head">Feels local, because it is</h2>
  <dl class="locals__grid">
    <div class="locals__item">
      <dt class="locals__term mono">cache-first</dt>
      <dd class="locals__body">
        Everything you've seen paints instantly from a local cache. The network
        refreshes quietly — every 60s and on focus.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="locals__item">
      <dt class="locals__term mono">resume</dt>
      <dd class="locals__body">
        Launch straight back into the last PR — the same file and scroll
        position you left it on.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="locals__item">
      <dt class="locals__term mono">notify</dt>
      <dd class="locals__body">
        A fresh review request pops a keyboard-dismissable toast. Enter opens
        it. No webhooks to set up.
      </dd>
    </div>
    <div class="locals__item">
      <dt class="locals__term mono">private</dt>
      <dd class="locals__body">
        No AI, no cloud. Your token stays in the Rust backend — it never
        reaches the webview.
      </dd>
    </div>
  </dl>
</section>
